James wrote:
> The hit points are usually manageable, except in the very
> earliest parts of the game.  The loss of strength isn't an issue
> if you have a means of restoring it.  Once you've got a Unicorn
> horn, you should be eating all poisonous corpses, unless your
> hit points are particularly low.  Even before then, if you have
> enough strength, it might be worthwhile.

Even without a unicorn horn, I've had a reasonable amount of success
getting poison resistance by putting a stack of heavy armor in a
closet, locking myself in, picking it up to become overtaxed, then
praying to fix the strength drain.  This is especially useful with
killer bees, since they appear in large enough groups that if you eat
them all you're nearly guaranteed to get both poison resistance and
strength 5.  Just be sure to move the armor before fighting them,
since otherwise your strength will be too low to move heavy gear
safely.  It's not entirely risk free, but the closet makes it a bit
safer than going without the resistance.




